00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,867
Theories must be tested.

299
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Inventions must be validated.

300
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,567
And some questions don't yet have

301
00:07:44,567 --> 00:07:46,367
answers. You can learn almost

302
00:07:46,367 --> 00:07:48,200
everything humanity has already

303
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,800
discovered. But to discover

304
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,100
something truly new...

305
00:07:51,333 --> 00:07:52,333
You still have to step into

306
00:07:52,333 --> 00:07:53,167
the unknown.

307
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:55,600
One year passes.

308
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,967
In that single year, you've

309
00:07:56,967 --> 00:07:58,433
absorbed an amount of knowledge

310
00:07:58,433 --> 00:07:59,633
that might once have taken a

311
00:07:59,633 --> 00:08:00,867
century of studying.

312
00:08:00,867 --> 00:08:01,767
But tonight...

313
00:08:01,767 --> 00:08:02,767
You're just having dinner with

314
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:03,367
your family.

315
00:08:03,367 --> 00:08:04,800
Your parents talk about work.

316
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:06,000
Your younger brother tells

317
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,467
everyone what happened at school.

318
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:08,667
You smile and listen.

319
00:08:08,667 --> 00:08:10,533
But your mind keeps analyzing

320
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:12,333
everything. You've become so

321
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:13,933
accustomed to understanding things

322
00:08:13,933 --> 00:08:15,333
almost instantly...

323
00:08:15,467 --> 00:08:17,267
That you've started to forget what

324
00:08:17,267 --> 00:08:19,233
struggling to learn actually feels

325
00:08:19,233 --> 00:08:20,433
like. And then...

326
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,133
You remember those evenings spent

327
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:23,567
staring at a difficult math

328
00:08:23,567 --> 00:08:25,333
problem. The frustration of

329
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:27,133
getting the answer wrong again and

330
00:08:27,133 --> 00:08:29,000
again. And the excitement when

331
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,800
everything finally made sense.

332
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,000
It's been a long time since

333
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,067
you've felt that way.

334
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:34,900
You've learned countless things.

335
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,367
Read thousands of books.

336
00:08:36,367 --> 00:08:38,133
Understood complicated theories.

337
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:39,633
Solved problems that once seemed

338
00:08:39,633 --> 00:08:41,233
impossible. But none of that

339
00:08:41,233 --> 00:08:43,167
automatically makes you happier.

340
00:08:43,167 --> 00:08:44,733
You can still feel exhausted.

341
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,667
Still make decisions you regret.

342
00:08:46,667 --> 00:08:48,133
And still face questions that no

343
00:08:48,133 --> 00:08:49,367
textbook can answer.

344
00:08:49,367 --> 00:08:50,900
For the first time, you wonder...

345
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,733
If everything becomes too easy...

346
00:08:52,867 --> 00:08:53,733
Will you still appreciate the

347
00:08:53,733 --> 00:08:54,667
journey of learning?

348
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:57,567
So, what would really happen if

349
00:08:57,567 --> 00:08:58,767
you could learn one hundred times

350
00:08:58,767 --> 00:09:00,667
faster? You could absorb knowledge

351
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:02,233
